<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Bagradas River (49 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/49-bce">49 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caesars-civil-war">Caesar's Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medjerda">Bagradas</a> River was fought in August 49 BCE in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, near the river now called the Medjerda in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>. Gaius Scribonius Curio, leading Caesar's invasion of Africa, was lured into an ambush by Saburra, general of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-i">Juba I of Numidia</a>, and his army was destroyed; Curio was killed. The victory kept Africa in Pompeian hands until 46 BCE.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 49 BCE Juba I destroyed the army of Gaius Scribonius Curio at the <b>Battle of the Bagradas River</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/numidia">Numidia · Military</a></li></ul></section>
